        "title": "asyncio-task"
      },
      "text": "sk groups combine a task creation API with a convenient\nand reliable way to wait for all tasks in the group to finish.\n\n.. class:: TaskGroup()\n\nAn :ref:`asynchronous context manager <async-context-managers>`\nholding a group of tasks.\nTasks can be added to the group using :meth:`create_task`.\nAll tasks are awaited when the context manager exits.\n\n.. versionadded:: 3.11\n\n.. method:: create_task(coro, *, name=None, context=None)\n\nCreate a task in this task group.\nThe signature matches that of :func:`asyncio.create_task`.\n\nExample::\n\nasync def main():\nasync with asyncio.TaskGroup() as tg:\ntask1 = tg.create_task(some_coro(...))\ntask2 = tg.create_task(another_coro(...))\nprint(f\"Both tasks have completed now: {task1.result()}, {task2.result()}\")\n\n",
      "text_sha256": "d2f4b4a9f11a03241e47ceb923a4a2c35f6d4ddd49526643ac65b7a06e2195a9",
      "grade": 2,
